zeroslike(::Type{M}, ax::Tuple{AbstractUnitRange, Vararg{AbstractUnitRange}}) where {M<:AbstractMatrix}
zeroslike(::Type{M}, sz::Tuple{Integer, Vararg{Integer}}) where {M<:AbstractMatrix}

Return an appropriate zero-ed array similar to M, with either the axes ax or
the size sz. This will be used as a structural zero element of a
matrix-valued banded matrix. By default, zeroslike falls back to using the
size along each axis to construct the array.
